<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait's KPI to sell lubricants to Texaco.</title>
<headline>Kuwait's KPI to sell lubricants to Texaco.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Kuwait Petroleum International Ltd (KPI) has signed a deal with Texaco Inc to sell the U.S. firm 317,500 tonnes of lubricants over five years, a Kuwait Petroleum Corp (KPC) official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;A deal has been signed to provide Texaco with lubricants,&quot; the official said of the deal that KPI, KPC's London-based subsidiary, signed with Texaco.</p>
<p>KPI will supply Texaco with 63,500 tonnes of lubricants per year over a five-year-span starting 1998, he said.</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan +965-243-1920</p>
